.{
    .name = .capnpc_zig,
    .version = "0.20.0",
    .minimum_zig_version = "0.17.0",
    .dependencies = .{
        // Pinned to a TAG, not a raw commit: tags are immutable release
        // points, so the pin is auditable and reproducible.
        //
        // v0.28.1 (commit 21d05d1): v0.28.0 with a build fix. v0.28.0 did not
        // compile for a 32-bit target (a comptime size assert in
        // `src/conn/RecvEndRing.zig`), so `-Dquic=true` failed for
        // x86-linux-gnu. v0.28.1 checks the record layout, not a fixed size.
        // There is no other change for a 64-bit target. Do not pin v0.28.0.
        //
        // v0.28.0 (commit a9078d8, skipped as a pin, included here): the end
        // of a stream is not lost when `tick` runs before the read.
        // `Connection.streamRecvEnd(id)` tells how the receive half of a
        // stream ended (a clean FIN, a reset and its code, or a stream that
        // the application stopped), before and after the `tick` that reclaims
        // it. The embedded seat and native mode read it. `quic.app` now
        // reports `.fin` or `.reset` for a stream that a `tick` reclaimed
        // first. A stream that the application stopped ends as `.reset` (the
        // peer answers the stop with RESET_STREAM) or `.reaped`, also while
        // it is live; `streamRecvEnd(id)` (null in the teardown pass for a
        // stream that has not ended) gives `stopped`. WHEN a stream is
        // reclaimed, when its credit returns, and the field
        // `Stream.recv.final_size` do not change. No wire change, no security
        // fix.
        //
        // v0.27.0 (commit 9d2ab6e): session tickets that live through a
        // restart. `Server.Config.session_ticket_key` and
        // `session_ticket_lifetime_s` replace the post-init install that
        // capnp-zig used to do on quic's TLS context, a `.pem` reload keeps
        // the key, `Server.rotateSessionTicketKey` changes it with no lost
        // ticket, and a client sends its 0-RTT data again after a Retry, so
        // a warm restore behind a Retry still runs before the handshake
        // completes (one round trip later). `Connection.retryAccepted()`
        // replaces our read of the `retry_accepted` field. A resumed client
        // can no longer open more early streams than the ticket remembers
        // (`StreamLimitExceeded`, transient, before the handshake).
        //
        // v0.26.0 (skipped as a pin, included here) repairs RFC 9000/9001
        // rules: Retry and NEW_TOKEN tokens are 114 bytes (were 96; an older
        // token reads as `.malformed`, which a server treats as no token:
        // one Retry, nothing closed); a server's close during the handshake
        // now reaches the client, so a refused session ends with
        // `DisconnectCause.peer_close`, not `.handshake_timeout`; and every
        // handshake datagram is at most 1200 bytes (a client Initial
        // exactly 1200).
        //
        // v0.25.0 was the SECURITY fix (one unauthenticated 12-byte
        // datagram could end a connection); v0.24.0 removed the 4096
        // lifetime stream cap (`initial_max_streams_*` is an open-at-once
        // window, see quic/options.zig `defaultTransportParams`); v0.21.1
        // freed the BoringSSL AEAD context leaked per handshake.
        //
        // ONE quic module per process: every package that links quic into
        // one build must pin the same tag and pass the same option map, or
        // the build makes two quic modules (and two BoringSSLs). The map is
        // `.target`, `.release`, `.@"sanitize-c" = "trap"` (build/modules.zig),
        // the one nest/qmsg/qmesh use. capnp-zig v0.20.0 pins v0.28.1; on
        // 2026-10-05 the main branches of qmsg and qmesh-zig, and nest, pin
        // v0.27.0. http3-zig cannot share this module at any pin: it builds
        // its own quic module from quic's src/root.zig and its own
        // BoringSSL. boringssl-zig is unchanged since v0.25.0: ff30fe99
        // (0.6.7, BoringSSL aef0e2df), which links Windows ws2_32 with
        // pkg-config lookup disabled.
        .quic = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/nullstyle/quic-zig/archive/refs/tags/v0.28.1.tar.gz",
            .hash = "quic-0.28.1-DnSYvacDOgCPlHPHQWufNaG2XMoKtnwwHJPVcIUuAmqB",
            .lazy = true,
        },
    },
    // Only what a downstream consumer needs to build the library + plugin.
    // vendor/ (git submodules that would dangle in a published archive),
    // tests/, bench/, tools/, and examples/ are development-only — the
    // library and plugin never import them at build time.
    .paths = .{
        "build.zig",
        "build.zig.zon",
        "build",
        "src",
        "README.md",
        "LICENSE",
    },
    .fingerprint = 0x9dca32f1156e479d,
}
